      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BILLS ANGEL (4) will find this an easier affair dropping from Saturday company after finishing 2.7L away from Cigar Man at Eagle Farm and she had FIERCE LUVA behind her on the course proper two starts ago. Sets up well with Youngberry's claim and is the one to beat. FIERCE LUVA (1) put it all together last start at Grafton when leading all the way over a longer trip. The form around him is stacking up and with confidence under his belt he can make it two on the bounce. GIDDY GAN'S JOY (5) is on a quick back-up after only warming late when resuming at the Sunshine Coast. Has enough staying substance, including a 2150m Ipswich win just before the break. No shock to see him charging at the business end. CHAYSE 'N' PENNY (2) hasn't fired in two runs over shorter trips but tackles a more suitable journey now and gets in well with Orr's 3kg claim. Not underestimating sharp improvement.",
